      "t": "Problem",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "Fees split across two accounts; wrong-account payments meant multi-day refunds, and reconciliation took 5 people two weeks per cycle.",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "Approach & key decisions",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "Implemented Route's predefined split rules so one student payment auto-distributed across both accounts. Webhooks reported success/failure in real time for immediate action; user-ID, payment-ID, and account-ID were mapped in a database for full traceability. Edge cases designed in: partial payments trigger a webhook prompt to the student; network failures surface instantly instead of silently desyncing books.",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "Results",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "−99% manual reconciliation effort, payments reconciled in real time with no mismatches, refund delays eliminated.",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "Specific internal data is summarised at the level Newton School permits publicly; happy to discuss details in conversation.",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
